{"app":"spr-flow","version":3,"nodes":[{"id":"note","type":"info","position":{"x":-910,"y":-543},"data":{"title":"Narrowband thermal emitter by simulated annealing (literature benchmark)","text":"H. Pan et al., Opt. Express 32, 47154 (2024). Air / Ge / SiO₂ / Ge / SiO₂ / Au 100 nm on Si: a quasi-Tamm emitter; emissivity = absorptance A (Kirchhoff).\n\nObjective (their eq. 6): F = a·FWHM/H + b·|1 − A_peak| + c/Q, here with a = 0.01 /nm, b = 1, c = 10 and a term d·|λ_peak − 5340 nm| (d = 0.005 /nm) that keeps the peak at 5.34 µm. Optimization Engine: simulated annealing (their settings: T₀ = 100, cooling 0.95, 1000 moves per temperature; here T₀ automatic, 50 moves per temperature, 4 chains).\n\nTheir optimum (351.1 / 998.9 / 392.6 / 1931.8 nm): A = 0.8261 at 5.34 µm, Q = 175. With Ge n = 4.0, SiO₂ Malitson n with k = 8.2·10⁻⁴ (mid-IR absorption; the paper takes its constants from the Handbook of Optics, not listed) and Au Drude (Ordal 1983) our TMM gives A ≈ 0.83 at 5.32 µm, Q ≈ 178. Set the Design variables to those values to check.\n\nStart: 400 / 1100 / 400 / 1800 nm (a weak peak at 5.15 µm). Press Start: the annealing moves the peak to 5.34 µm and narrows it (A ≈ 0.85, Q ≈ 225 in about 12 000 evaluations).","color":"#8a93a6","width":400,"height":380}},{"id":"air","type":"material","position":{"x":-910,"y":-47},"data":{"materialId":"Air","color":"#f4f6fa","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"ge","type":"material","position":{"x":-910,"y":153},"data":{"materialId":"user-ge-ir","color":"#7b7f86","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"sio2","type":"material","position":{"x":-910,"y":354},"data":{"materialId":"user-sio2-ir","color":"#9ec5e8","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"au","type":"material","position":{"x":-910,"y":555},"data":{"materialId":"user-au-drude","color":"#d4af37","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"si","type":"material","position":{"x":-910,"y":755},"data":{"materialId":"user-si-ir","color":"#5a6270","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"v1","type":"variable","position":{"x":-1352,"y":71},"data":{"name":"d Ge (top)","value":400,"min":50,"max":1000,"integer":false}},{"id":"v2","type":"variable","position":{"x":-1352,"y":307},"data":{"name":"d SiO₂ (1)","value":1100,"min":200,"max":2500,"integer":false}},{"id":"v3","type":"variable","position":{"x":-1352,"y":543},"data":{"name":"d Ge (2)","value":400,"min":50,"max":1000,"integer":false}},{"id":"v4","type":"variable","position":{"x":-1352,"y":779},"data":{"name":"d SiO₂ (2)","value":1800,"min":200,"max":3000,"integer":false}},{"id":"l1","type":"layer","position":{"x":-494,"y":-24},"data":{"label":"Ge","thickness":400,"layers2D":1}},{"id":"l2","type":"layer","position":{"x":-494,"y":165},"data":{"label":"SiO₂","thickness":1100,"layers2D":1}},{"id":"l3","type":"layer","position":{"x":-494,"y":354},"data":{"label":"Ge","thickness":400,"layers2D":1}},{"id":"l4","type":"layer","position":{"x":-494,"y":543},"data":{"label":"SiO₂","thickness":1800,"layers2D":1}},{"id":"l5","type":"layer","position":{"x":-494,"y":732},"data":{"label":"Au","thickness":100,"layers2D":1}},{"id":"stack","type":"combine","position":{"x":52,"y":71},"data":{"name":"Quasi-Tamm emitter","count":5}},{"id":"wl","type":"param","position":{"x":52,"y":543},"data":{"quantity":"lambda","mode":"range","value":5340,"min":4800,"max":6000,"step":0.5}},{"id":"th","type":"param","position":{"x":52,"y":802},"data":{"quantity":"theta","mode":"constant","value":0,"min":0,"max":80,"step":1}},{"id":"tmm","type":"compute","position":{"x":598,"y":71},"data":{"name":"Emitter","polarization":"s"}},{"id":"fwhm","type":"fwhm","position":{"x":1144,"y":-71},"data":{"kind":"peak","field":"A","along":"lambda","method":"local","level":0.5,"intervals":[{"lo":5000,"hi":5700}],"color":"#f28e2b"}},{"id":"obj","type":"formula","position":{"x":1690,"y":-71},"data":{"name":"F (Pan et al., eq. 6)","goal":"min","weight":1,"terms":[{"name":"w","source":"fwhm:metrics","field":"w0","stat":"mean"},{"name":"H","source":"fwhm:metrics","field":"e0","stat":"mean"},{"name":"Q","source":"fwhm:metrics","field":"q0","stat":"mean"},{"name":"lp","source":"fwhm:metrics","field":"c0","stat":"mean"}],"expr":"0.01*abs(w/H) + abs(1 - H) + 10/Q + 0.005*abs(lp - 5340)"}},{"id":"opt","type":"optimizer","position":{"x":2236,"y":-71},"data":{"algorithm":"sa","iterations":3000,"population":30,"lr":0.05,"starts":4,"seed":1,"polish":true,"preview":false,"disabled":[],"runs":[],"outputRun":"","outputPoint":-1,"outputCompute":"","startFromOutput":false}},{"id":"plot","type":"plot","position":{"x":1144,"y":496},"data":{"field":"A","mode":"auto","x":"","y":"","series":"","seriesSel":null,"fixed":{},"autoY":false}},{"id":"plotOpt","type":"plot","position":{"x":2236,"y":661},"data":{"field":"A","mode":"auto","x":"","y":"","series":"","seriesSel":null,"fixed":{},"autoY":false}}],"edges":[{"id":"e-air-out-stack-incident","source":"air","sourceHandle":"out","target":"stack","targetHandle":"incident"},{"id":"e-si-out-stack-exit","source":"si","sourceHandle":"out","target":"stack","targetHandle":"exit"},{"id":"e-ge-out-l1-mat","source":"ge","sourceHandle":"out","target":"l1","targetHandle":"mat"},{"id":"e-sio2-out-l2-mat","source":"sio2","sourceHandle":"out","target":"l2","targetHandle":"mat"},{"id":"e-ge-out-l3-mat","source":"ge","sourceHandle":"out","target":"l3","targetHandle":"mat"},{"id":"e-sio2-out-l4-mat","source":"sio2","sourceHandle":"out","target":"l4","targetHandle":"mat"},{"id":"e-au-out-l5-mat","source":"au","sourceHandle":"out","target":"l5","targetHandle":"mat"},{"id":"e-v1-out-l1-d","source":"v1","sourceHandle":"out","target":"l1","targetHandle":"d"},{"id":"e-v2-out-l2-d","source":"v2","sourceHandle":"out","target":"l2","targetHandle":"d"},{"id":"e-v3-out-l3-d","source":"v3","sourceHandle":"out","target":"l3","targetHandle":"d"},{"id":"e-v4-out-l4-d","source":"v4","sourceHandle":"out","target":"l4","targetHandle":"d"},{"id":"e-l1-out-stack-item-0","source":"l1","sourceHandle":"out","target":"stack","targetHandle":"item-0"},{"id":"e-l2-out-stack-item-1","source":"l2","sourceHandle":"out","target":"stack","targetHandle":"item-1"},{"id":"e-l3-out-stack-item-2","source":"l3","sourceHandle":"out","target":"stack","targetHandle":"item-2"},{"id":"e-l4-out-stack-item-3","source":"l4","sourceHandle":"out","target":"stack","targetHandle":"item-3"},{"id":"e-l5-out-stack-item-4","source":"l5","sourceHandle":"out","target":"stack","targetHandle":"item-4"},{"id":"e-stack-out-tmm-stack","source":"stack","sourceHandle":"out","target":"tmm","targetHandle":"stack"},{"id":"e-wl-out-tmm-lambda","source":"wl","sourceHandle":"out","target":"tmm","targetHandle":"lambda"},{"id":"e-th-out-tmm-theta","source":"th","sourceHandle":"out","target":"tmm","targetHandle":"theta"},{"id":"e-tmm-out-fwhm-in","source":"tmm","sourceHandle":"out","target":"fwhm","targetHandle":"in"},{"id":"e-fwhm-metrics-obj-in","source":"fwhm","sourceHandle":"metrics","target":"obj","targetHandle":"in"},{"id":"e-obj-out-opt-obj","source":"obj","sourceHandle":"out","target":"opt","targetHandle":"obj"},{"id":"e-tmm-out-plot-in","source":"tmm","sourceHandle":"out","target":"plot","targetHandle":"in"},{"id":"e-opt-out-plotOpt-in","source":"opt","sourceHandle":"out","target":"plotOpt","targetHandle":"in"}],"materials":[{"id":"user-ge-ir","name":"Ge (IR, n = 4.0)","color":"#7b7f86","model":{"type":"constant","n":4,"k":0},"source":"germanium in the mid-infrared, n ≈ 4.0 (Handbook of Optics); constant approximation"},{"id":"user-sio2-ir","name":"SiO₂ (mid-IR, k = 8.2e-4)","color":"#9ec5e8","model":{"type":"formula","formula":1,"coefficients":[0,0.6961663,0.0684043,0.4079426,0.1162414,0.8974794,9.896161],"k":0.00082},"source":"n: Malitson (1965) dispersion formula; k = 8.2·10⁻⁴: weak mid-IR absorption chosen so that the published optimum of Pan et al. (2024) gives their peak absorptance (calibration)"},{"id":"user-au-drude","name":"Au (D